Welcome! This is the first post on a blog about **artificial intelligence**: models, tools, research papers, and what it all means.

## How this site works

The whole thing is open source, and every post lives in a git repo:

- Posts are Markdown (Markdoc) files in a git repo.
- [Astro](https://astro.build) turns them into static HTML.
- [Keystatic](https://keystatic.com) provides a local editor at `/keystatic`.
- GitHub Pages hosts the built site, and GitHub Actions redeploys on every push.

```python
from anthropic import Anthropic

client = Anthropic()
msg = client.messages.create(
    model="claude-opus-5-5",
    max_tokens=256,
    messages=[{"role": "user", "content": "Say hello to my readers."}],
)
print(msg.content[0].text)
```

> Delete this post and write your own, either in the editor or by adding a `.mdoc` file to `src/content/posts/`.
